 * block the publisher or other subscribers (decoupling publish() from consumption).
 *
 * Node is single-threaded, so "concurrency" here means interleaved async consumer loops
 * (via setImmediate) rather than OS threads -- the same bounded-queue-per-subscriber
 * design guards against one subscriber starving another, and enqueue/ack/nack are each
 * atomic within a single synchronous turn of the event loop.
